# Consumer table — the source of per-consumer identity.
#
#   <consumer-name>  <credential>
#
# The credential is compared by key-auth against the RAW value of the
# Authorization header, with no Bearer stripping (main.go looks the whole
# header value up in credential2Name), so it must include the "Bearer " prefix
# exactly as the client sends it.
#
# Copy to consumers.conf and fill in real keys. consumers.conf is gitignored.
#
# `legacy-shared` MUST hold the current EDGE_API_KEY value from
# ../qwen3.6-27b-2-A100/.env — that is what keeps every existing client working
# unchanged when a public hostname is eventually pointed at this gateway.
# It is retired only once its traffic counter has been flat at zero.

legacy-shared   Bearer sk-REPLACE-with-the-current-EDGE_API_KEY
quota-admin     Bearer sk-REPLACE-admin-key-for-quota-management
danila          Bearer sk-REPLACE-per-person-key
